# N9 Bounded Display Observation

You are the single fresh independent observer for the assigned batch only.
The parent supplies a batch number. All shell commands MUST explicitly use
workdir `/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-182-six/lemmadeck`.
You are not alone; do not modify files owned by others.

Read the Image batches section in `.agents/skills/ld-s10y-image/SKILL.md`
and `.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/references/production-resume.md`.
The parent has already completed ticket setup and authority reads. Do not
reinitialize, query a backend, open another chat, start agents, use network/DB,
read `.env`, render, validate, solve math, read answers/keys or source figures.

Input:
`.tmp/resume182-6-n9-display-selection-FIRST/batch<N>.json`.
Output:
`.tmp/resume182-6-n9-display-observe-batch<N>/result.json`.

Read only the bounded batch metadata and verify every assigned PNG SHA.
View each assigned native PNG exactly ONCE using `view_image`.
No reopens, crops, resizing, alternate screenshots or images outside this batch.
Max 8 images per batch and 24 per context.
Check actual visible text/formulas/tables/figure pixels for legibility,
collisions, blank content, permanent internal clipping and unintended layout.
Native viewport-edge cropping and intentional horizontal-scroll windows are
expected. Metadata may locate a window but cannot approve unseen pixels.
Do not call a partial scroll window permanent loss without visible evidence.
This is display-only, not a re-review of approved mathematics.

Create the output directory with `mkdir` if needed and write the new result
using `apply_patch`. Required schema:

```json
{
  "status": "DISPLAY_PASS or DISPLAY_FAIL",
  "blockers": [],
  "images": [
    {
      "path": "absolute assigned path",
      "sha256": "assigned hash",
      "observations": ["concrete textual visual observations"],
      "blockers": []
    }
  ],
  "imageAccounting": {
    "views": 8,
    "uniqueImages": 8,
    "reopens": 0,
    "crops": 0,
    "resizes": 0,
    "rerenders": 0
  }
}
```

Use actual assigned counts. Record defects honestly. Preserve tool errors and
unknown host token/cost accounting as unknown; never reset actual counts.
Return only textual verdict, output absolute path, SHA and counts. Do not
return image payloads to the parent. Stop after this batch; no prefetch.
